title: karr init gitignores tasks/ and config.yml even when those paths are already
  tracked
updated: 2026-08-10T03:55:23Z
---

Found while fixing #48.

`karr init` appends `tasks/` and `config.yml` to .gitignore unconditionally. If
the repository already tracks files at those paths, git ignores the ignore rule
for them — tracked files stay tracked — so nothing breaks. But the .gitignore
now claims something that is not true, and anyone reading it concludes karr owns
those paths when the project does.

It also interacts with the #48 fix: materialize now refuses to overwrite what
git tracks, so a repo in this state gets a refusal from a command whose
.gitignore entry suggests the path is karr-owned. The error is correct and the
.gitignore is what misleads.

Fix: only add an entry when nothing is tracked at that path, or word it so the
situation is visible. `App::karr::Git::is_tracked` (added for #48) already
answers the question.
Geschlossen durch cd4d043/58f0fc7: init laesst .gitignore in Ruhe, wenn das Projekt die Pfade schon trackt, und sagt das auch. Offen geblieben (im Ticket-Text vermerkt): materialize macht denselben Check noch nicht. t/109.
